86517094 1074 "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\csc x.$\n\n![](images/f1/f1b80c29b8f9f4d33aae94fc287d95b97cc5865b36ecc98f4f41e625dfc842e1.png)\n\nNow, let's go through each statement.\n\n- The cosecant takes the value $1$ at $x=\\frac{9\\pi }{2}$. Hence, statement I is false.\n\n- The lines $x=n\\pi$ for any integer $n$ are the vertical asymptotes of the function. Hence, statement II is true.\n\n- The domain excludes exactly the integer multiples of $\\pi$. The number $\\frac{7\\pi }{2}$ is not an integer multiple of $\\pi$. Hence, statement III is true." 13194139535558 17592186045443 true] [17592186517095 1068 #edb/ref 17592186516987 13194139535558 17592186045443 true] [17592186517095 1068 #edb/ref 17592186517004 13194139535558 17592186045443 true] [17592186517095 1068 #edb/ref 17592186517034 13194139535558 17592186045443 true] [17592186517095 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139535558 17592186045443 true] [17592186517095 1071 "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\csc x$?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The point $(\\frac{9\\pi }{2},-1)$ is on the graph.\n- **II.** $x=-3\\pi $ is a vertical asymptote.\n- **III.** $x=\\frac{-4\\pi }{2}$ is in the domain." 13194139535558 17592186045443 true] [17592186517095 1072 #uuid "fb8b6ba6-3782-5361-89b1-1ab426047925" 13194139535558 17592186045443 true] [17592186517095 1074 "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\csc x.$\n\n![](images/f1/f1b80c29b8f9f4d33aae94fc287d95b97cc5865b36ecc98f4f41e625dfc842e1.png)\n\nNow, let's go through each statement.\n\n- The cosecant takes the value $1$ at $x=\\frac{9\\pi }{2}$. Hence, statement I is false.\n\n- The lines $x=n\\pi$ for any integer $n$ are the vertical asymptotes of the function. Hence, statement II is true.\n\n- The domain excludes exactly the integer multiples of $\\pi$. The number $\\frac{-4\\pi }{2}$ is an integer multiple of $\\pi$. Hence, statement III is false." 13194139535558 17592186045443 true] [17592186517096 1080 "false" 13194139535558 17592186